--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- composite chain + SYROPE polyester + chain mooring on a moving vessel
-- One LINE of three SECTIONS in End-A(fairlead)->End-B(anchor) order: a 100 m studless chain
-- at the fairlead, a 400 m polyester section with the Syrope working-curve model, and a 250 m
-- chain at the anchor, in 200 m of water. The line of composite_chain_poly_chain.dat with its
-- anchor 30 m further out, so the polyester carries about 1 MN. The polyester's EA and BA
-- columns, its settings and OWC files, are those of syrope_polyester_mooring.dat. The static
-- start puts every polyester element on its rest curve (here the OWC: the rope is virgin), so
-- the dynamics start in that equilibrium. The vessel then surges, heaves and pitches in the
-- 12 s record of lazy_wave_vessel_motion.dat, with its 12 s smooth start.
--   chain 155 mm R4 studless: volume-equivalent diam 0.2791 m, dry mass 480.93 kg/m, EA 2.058e9 N.
--   polyester 181.8 mm: diam 0.1438 m, dry mass 22.42 kg/m.
